1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,000
After his triumph, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Top 200

5
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:02,840
minimum

6
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:04,720
casual

7
00:01:04,720 --> 00:01:07,160
.

8
00:01:07,220 --> 00:01:10,780
.

9
00:01:10,780 --> 00:01:16,720
.

10
00:01:16,720 --> 00:01:18,660
.

11
00:01:18,660 --> 00:01:25,240
遥か未来へ 今駆け出したんだ

12
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:29,940
まだ見ぬ不安すら全て越えて

13
00:01:29,940 --> 00:01:35,820
あの日描いた僕が僕であるために

14
00:01:35,820 --> 00:01:40,060
見つぬけてページの続けが強

15
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:44,740
君と言う希望と言う

16
00:01:44,740 --> 00:01:49,740
It's like a one page, like you and me.

17
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:52,740
Do you want to call me this?

18
00:02:14,740 --> 00:02:19,740
It's incredibly crumbly and mealy,

19
00:02:19,740 --> 00:02:23,740
and I'm not certain I've ever had something that dries the mouth so.

20
00:02:25,740 --> 00:02:28,740
And yet it's tasty.

21
00:02:28,740 --> 00:02:31,740
Good. I'm so glad to hear it.

22
00:02:31,740 --> 00:02:36,740
Sister Lily, it seems you possess an exemplary talent for cooking.

23
00:02:36,740 --> 00:02:38,740
I only prepared a few basic dishes.

24
00:02:38,740 --> 00:02:40,740
There's more than enough for everyone.

25
00:02:40,740 --> 00:02:42,740
Don't hesitate to eat as much as you'd like.

26
00:02:42,740 --> 00:02:44,740
And the same goes for you two as well, of course.

27
00:02:44,740 --> 00:02:47,740
Yes, thank you.

28
00:02:47,740 --> 00:02:49,740
A noble of the Clover Kingdom,

29
00:02:49,740 --> 00:02:53,740
and a ramshackle church eating dishes that defy identification.

30
00:02:53,740 --> 00:02:56,740
Oh wow, it truly does dry one's mouth out.

31
00:02:56,740 --> 00:02:58,740
Yes, quite extraordinary, isn't it?

32
00:02:58,740 --> 00:03:04,740
Our good boys, Yuno and Asta, both sent home money from the first wages they received as Magic Knights.

33
00:03:04,740 --> 00:03:08,740
Thanks to them, we were able to buy a huge supply of pot potatoes,

34
00:03:08,740 --> 00:03:13,740
enough to make sure all the children here at the church will have full bellies every day.

35
00:03:13,740 --> 00:03:18,740
Here's an idea. Maybe next time buy us something different for once.

36
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:21,740
There's no need to be greedy, Nash.

37
00:03:21,740 --> 00:03:25,740
Just look at how big and strong Yuno here got on a steady diet of pot potatoes.

38
00:03:25,740 --> 00:03:31,740
Yuno, sending the first of your wages back home, that was very honorable.

39
00:03:31,740 --> 00:03:33,740
It's nothing.

40
00:03:33,740 --> 00:03:34,740
That's not true.

41
00:03:34,740 --> 00:03:36,740
We're very grateful, Yuno.

42
00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:39,740
The money that you sent helped us out so much.

43
00:03:39,740 --> 00:03:41,740
And not just with pot potatoes.

44
00:03:41,740 --> 00:03:43,740
We were finally able to patch up all the holes in the floor.

45
00:03:43,740 --> 00:03:45,740
We dug a well out in the garden, too.

46
00:03:45,740 --> 00:03:47,740
Thank you for everything, Yuno!

47
00:03:47,740 --> 00:03:48,740
Yeah, for everything!

48
00:03:51,740 --> 00:03:53,740
Asta sent something, too?

49
00:03:53,740 --> 00:03:57,740
Yes! And what a contribution it was!

50
00:04:01,740 --> 00:04:02,740
How much did he send?

51
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:06,740
Oh, um… he… uh…

52
00:04:12,740 --> 00:04:14,740
Beat you, Yuno!

53
00:04:14,740 --> 00:04:18,740
When I get my wages next month, I'm sending it all to you.

54
00:04:18,740 --> 00:04:19,740
What?

55
00:04:19,740 --> 00:04:21,740
That really isn't necessary.

56
00:04:21,740 --> 00:04:23,740
The amount you already sent was so generous.

57
00:04:23,740 --> 00:04:25,740
We'll be more than fine for a while.

58
00:04:25,740 --> 00:04:27,740
But thank you for offering.

59
00:04:27,740 --> 00:04:28,740
You'll get it all.

60
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:31,740
Um… well… sure.

61
00:04:31,740 --> 00:04:33,740
If that's what you want…

62
00:04:34,740 --> 00:04:35,740
Pardon, Salim sir.

63
00:04:35,740 --> 00:04:37,740
We really ought to be on our way now.

64
00:04:37,740 --> 00:04:39,740
Why, what's the hurry?

65
00:04:39,740 --> 00:04:41,740
We can stay a little longer, surely.

66
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:43,740
Just think, as members of the nobility,

67
00:04:43,740 --> 00:04:47,740
we have a rare opportunity to broaden our horizons here.

68
00:04:47,740 --> 00:04:49,740
Please, Sister Lily.

69
00:04:49,740 --> 00:04:51,740
Might I trouble you for another glass of water?

70
00:04:51,740 --> 00:04:52,740
Of course!

71
00:04:55,740 --> 00:04:56,740
Looks like it's empty.

72
00:04:57,740 --> 00:04:58,740
Well, I'll go.

73
00:04:59,740 --> 00:05:00,740
Let me…

74
00:05:00,740 --> 00:05:01,740
No, it's alright.

75
00:05:01,740 --> 00:05:03,740
You just stay put and relax.

76
00:05:05,740 --> 00:05:06,740
Wait, please.

77
00:05:06,740 --> 00:05:07,740
Just a moment.

78
00:05:11,740 --> 00:05:13,740
It still gets rather chilly out at night.

79
00:05:14,740 --> 00:05:16,740
Thank you very much.

80
00:05:17,740 --> 00:05:21,740
A real gentleman, aren't you?

81
00:05:21,740 --> 00:05:22,740
Yes, well, you know.

82
00:05:22,740 --> 00:05:24,740
These things just come naturally to me.

83
00:05:24,740 --> 00:05:27,740
That's what it means to be a true nobleman.

84
00:05:27,740 --> 00:05:28,740
What happened?

85
00:05:28,740 --> 00:05:29,740
What was that crash?

86
00:05:29,740 --> 00:05:30,740
Where's Sister Lily?

87
00:05:30,740 --> 00:05:31,740
I recognize that.

88
00:05:31,740 --> 00:05:32,740
The villains who killed her,

89
00:05:32,740 --> 00:05:33,740
uh…

90
00:05:33,740 --> 00:05:34,740
uh…

91
00:05:34,740 --> 00:05:35,740
Uh…

92
00:05:35,740 --> 00:05:36,740
Uh…

93
00:05:36,740 --> 00:05:37,740
uh…

94
00:05:37,740 --> 00:05:38,740
Uh…

95
00:05:38,740 --> 00:05:39,740
Uh…

96
00:05:39,740 --> 00:05:40,740
Uh…

97
00:05:40,740 --> 00:05:41,740
Uh…

98
00:05:41,740 --> 00:05:42,740
Uh…

99
00:05:42,740 --> 00:05:43,740
Uh…

100
00:05:43,740 --> 00:05:44,740
Uh…

101
00:05:44,740 --> 00:05:45,740
Uh…

102
00:05:45,740 --> 00:05:46,740
Uh…

103
00:05:46,740 --> 00:05:47,740
Uh…

104
00:05:47,740 --> 00:05:48,740
What happened?!

105
00:05:48,740 --> 00:05:49,740
What was that crash?!

106
00:05:49,740 --> 00:05:51,740
Where's Sister Lily?!

107
00:05:51,740 --> 00:05:59,740
I recognize that

108
00:05:59,740 --> 00:06:03,160
The villains who came after Selim before were wearing these brooches

109
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:05,120
Those bandits who attacked us earlier?

110
00:06:05,560 --> 00:06:06,780
I can't believe it

111
00:06:06,780 --> 00:06:09,600
I gave her my robe so she wouldn't catch cold out here

112
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:13,760
But because she was wearing it, they took Sister Lily mistaking her for me

113
00:06:13,760 --> 00:06:16,980
Oh, it makes sense

114
00:06:16,980 --> 00:06:18,380
That must be what happened

115
00:06:18,380 --> 00:06:22,260
Is Sister Lily going to be okay?

116
00:06:22,780 --> 00:06:25,300
Is she? You know? You know?

117
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:28,820
Yes, don't worry

118
00:06:28,820 --> 00:06:31,300
I'll bring her back

119
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:35,140
I'm going to

120
00:06:35,140 --> 00:06:36,240
Yeah, so am I

121
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:37,140
Count me in

122
00:06:37,140 --> 00:06:38,520
No

123
00:06:38,520 --> 00:06:41,160
Everyone else stays here

124
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:43,460
I can handle this on my own

125
00:06:43,460 --> 00:06:46,520
Hold on

126
00:06:46,520 --> 00:06:48,940
Remember our mission

127
00:06:48,940 --> 00:06:50,420
To protect Selim

128
00:06:50,420 --> 00:06:52,820
We don't know when they'll come for him again

129
00:06:52,820 --> 00:06:56,000
We must depart at once

130
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,660
You can't really mean that

131
00:06:57,660 --> 00:06:59,200
What about Sister?

132
00:06:59,780 --> 00:07:01,240
Yeah, come on, Four Eyes

133
00:07:01,240 --> 00:07:02,600
What did you just call me?

134
00:07:03,400 --> 00:07:04,320
Um, Four Eyes

135
00:07:04,320 --> 00:07:06,280
I mean, Klaus

136
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:07,380
Can't we?

137
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:09,500
That's quite enough, Mimosa

138
00:07:09,500 --> 00:07:13,040
Now, I know you're worried about your friend

139
00:07:13,040 --> 00:07:15,800
But you will just have to leave it for the local watch to handle

140
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:17,700
We're leaving this instant

141
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:21,420
Come, I need everybody to move quickly

142
00:07:21,420 --> 00:07:22,460
Let's go

143
00:07:22,460 --> 00:07:25,140
Yes, sir

144
00:07:25,140 --> 00:07:26,060
You know?

145
00:07:27,140 --> 00:07:28,020
No, sir

146
00:07:28,020 --> 00:07:31,660
You will do your duty

147
00:07:31,660 --> 00:07:33,980
Insubordination will be punished

148
00:07:33,980 --> 00:07:35,320
Be that as it may

149
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:37,200
I'm going after her

150
00:07:37,200 --> 00:07:41,460
You know

151
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:45,700
Does whatever he pleases

152
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:59,220
Did no one ever tell you that recklessness isn't the same as bravery?

153
00:07:59,780 --> 00:08:00,500
You know

154
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:02,880
He knows my name

155
00:08:02,880 --> 00:08:06,440
How about I show you the difference?

156
00:08:07,200 --> 00:08:11,200
Towering tornado

157
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:13,500
What's that?

158
00:08:17,500 --> 00:08:18,700
That's one down

159
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:20,700
Four to go

160
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:31,440
I'm not necessarily gonna kill you

161
00:08:31,440 --> 00:08:32,520
So don't worry

162
00:08:32,520 --> 00:08:34,280
This might hurt just a little bit, though

163
00:08:34,280 --> 00:08:34,820
Sorry

164
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:37,180
I see what's going on here

165
00:08:37,180 --> 00:08:39,800
It's me you've been after this whole time

166
00:08:39,800 --> 00:08:40,860
Not Salim

167
00:08:40,860 --> 00:08:44,560
You really are a clever boy, aren't you?

168
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:52,440
Now I'll sit back and watch you drown

169
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:57,020
I don't know what you're talking about

170
00:08:57,020 --> 00:08:58,620
I can breathe here just fine

171
00:08:58,620 --> 00:08:59,120
What the?

172
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:04,540
If you want to know how to drown someone

173
00:09:04,540 --> 00:09:07,180
Let me show you

174
00:09:07,180 --> 00:09:19,440
That's two down

175
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:19,460
That's two down

176
00:09:19,460 --> 00:09:41,160
I can't believe you fell for our false trail so weaselly

177
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:43,520
How do you like that?

178
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:44,020
How do you like that?

179
00:09:46,640 --> 00:09:47,960
Not bad

180
00:09:47,960 --> 00:09:49,200
Let's see

181
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:54,460
How about this?

182
00:09:54,460 --> 00:10:02,200
Impossible

183
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:05,940
What is it about people like you?

184
00:10:05,940 --> 00:10:08,440
You always seem to think that bigger is better

185
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:10,280
Fine, I'll just

186
00:10:10,280 --> 00:10:10,840
Too late

187
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:15,840
Three down

188
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:18,000
Just two to go

189
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:33,540
That's sister Lily

190
00:10:33,540 --> 00:10:35,940
Stop right there

191
00:10:35,940 --> 00:10:38,040
That's a good boy

192
00:10:38,040 --> 00:10:40,400
You wouldn't want to do anything stupid

193
00:10:40,400 --> 00:10:43,300
And get the sister's pretty face burned now, would you?

194
00:10:43,300 --> 00:11:04,300
You know

195
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:08,320
Even as young as you are, you seem to have a real talent for magic

196
00:11:08,320 --> 00:11:13,280
If you ever see someone in trouble, please help them instead of looking the other way

197
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:15,160
Promise me

198
00:11:15,160 --> 00:11:17,400
You too, Austin

199
00:11:17,400 --> 00:11:18,460
What, sister Lily?

200
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:19,960
Did you say something?

201
00:11:25,400 --> 00:11:27,260
Now then, down to business

202
00:11:27,260 --> 00:11:29,780
And over that grimoire of yours, you know

203
00:11:29,780 --> 00:11:33,400
Without it, you should be suitably helpless

204
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:36,420
What would you do with my grimoire?

205
00:11:36,760 --> 00:11:37,660
Sell it, perhaps?

206
00:11:38,380 --> 00:11:40,220
Maybe I'll decide to burn it instead

207
00:11:40,220 --> 00:11:43,220
I'm not especially concerned about what becomes of it

208
00:11:43,220 --> 00:11:47,780
If you don't have your grimoire, the magic knights won't see any reason to keep you around

209
00:11:47,780 --> 00:11:50,140
Is that what you're after?

210
00:11:50,140 --> 00:11:54,560
And if I won't give it up?

211
00:11:55,020 --> 00:11:55,700
You're refusing?

212
00:12:01,960 --> 00:12:03,100
That's what I thought

213
00:12:03,100 --> 00:12:04,440
Hand it over

214
00:12:04,440 --> 00:12:07,940
Then you can take your precious sister and be on your way

215
00:12:07,940 --> 00:12:11,320
Not happening

216
00:12:11,320 --> 00:12:11,920
What?

217
00:12:12,460 --> 00:12:13,720
Don't you understand?

218
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:14,500
She'll be

219
00:12:14,500 --> 00:12:16,020
I'm not going to let you hurt her

220
00:12:16,020 --> 00:12:18,540
You think attacking me is going to do any good?

221
00:12:18,880 --> 00:12:20,360
If you want to give it a shot, okay?

222
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:20,940
Sure

223
00:12:20,940 --> 00:12:22,600
I won't be the one attacking

224
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:23,880
Who?

225
00:12:25,160 --> 00:12:25,720
Right!

226
00:12:25,940 --> 00:12:27,240
Steel creation magic!

227
00:12:27,540 --> 00:12:28,500
Spiral lance!

228
00:12:37,220 --> 00:12:37,860
Mimosa

229
00:12:37,860 --> 00:12:38,680
Right!

230
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:43,900
She'll be okay

231
00:12:43,900 --> 00:12:47,420
Are any of the bandits unaccounted for?

232
00:12:47,500 --> 00:12:49,440
By my count, there should be one more of them

233
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:50,820
Ran away then

234
00:12:50,820 --> 00:12:57,280
What were you planning on doing if I hadn't been there to help?

235
00:12:58,580 --> 00:12:59,900
Why are you here?

236
00:13:00,840 --> 00:13:03,360
Honestly, you know, do you take me for some kind of fool?

237
00:13:05,060 --> 00:13:06,520
He does, the brat!

238
00:13:08,340 --> 00:13:09,580
Now listen closely

239
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:12,020
As magic knights, we have a solemn duty

240
00:13:12,020 --> 00:13:13,820
To safeguard the people

241
00:13:13,820 --> 00:13:18,440
I already suspected something was off

242
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:22,120
This bunch wasn't out for Salim

243
00:13:22,120 --> 00:13:23,500
They were after you

244
00:13:23,500 --> 00:13:28,400
You imagine a noble would want to visit this village

245
00:13:28,400 --> 00:13:31,020
That he'd eat pop potatoes and without complaint?

246
00:13:31,020 --> 00:13:35,400
I'm sorry, but I don't think so

247
00:13:35,400 --> 00:13:39,920
And they didn't abduct the sister thinking she was Salim

248
00:13:39,920 --> 00:13:41,080
Rubbish

249
00:13:41,080 --> 00:13:46,280
I found it strange that Salim would want you as his bodyguard after losing to you

250
00:13:46,280 --> 00:13:48,800
After you left to rescue sister Lily

251
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:49,960
I used a spell on Salim

252
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:53,180
My plant creation magic, flower of truth

253
00:13:53,180 --> 00:13:57,900
It's Yuno's fault that I didn't get to join the magic knights

254
00:13:57,900 --> 00:14:00,260
Him and that four-leaf clover grimoire

255
00:14:00,260 --> 00:14:01,280
Damn book!

256
00:14:01,540 --> 00:14:03,260
I'm going to take it from him!

257
00:14:04,020 --> 00:14:07,080
He'll know what real pain is by the time daddy gets through with him

258
00:14:07,080 --> 00:14:09,240
I will have my revenge!

259
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:11,920
He gave up everything easily

260
00:14:11,920 --> 00:14:16,420
But once you decided to come find me, how'd you know where to look?

261
00:14:16,780 --> 00:14:18,800
That was Mimosa's doing as well

262
00:14:18,800 --> 00:14:21,720
Plant creation magic

263
00:14:21,720 --> 00:14:23,780
Magic flower guidepost

264
00:14:23,780 --> 00:14:26,560
Let's see

265
00:14:26,560 --> 00:14:28,780
Oh yes, there they are

266
00:14:28,780 --> 00:14:34,540
And that's how we were able to arrive just in time to provide backup

267
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:37,780
I'm very glad you came

268
00:14:37,780 --> 00:14:39,360
I needed the help

269
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:40,980
Thank you, Klaus

270
00:14:40,980 --> 00:14:42,080
Mimosa

271
00:14:42,080 --> 00:14:44,920
It's nothing

272
00:14:44,920 --> 00:14:47,720
Quiet!

273
00:14:48,840 --> 00:14:49,440
Honestly

274
00:14:49,440 --> 00:14:51,880
Blaming others for your own failure?

275
00:14:52,220 --> 00:14:54,520
Obviously you'd be the loser in a match against Yuno

276
00:14:54,520 --> 00:14:58,780
He earned the approval of all the squad captains

277
00:14:58,780 --> 00:15:01,500
Chief among them, Captain William Vongence

278
00:15:01,500 --> 00:15:03,580
Leader of the Great Golden Dawn

279
00:15:03,580 --> 00:15:06,620
That should tell you how talented he is

280
00:15:06,620 --> 00:15:07,880
Thank you, sir

281
00:15:07,880 --> 00:15:10,300
Yes

282
00:15:10,300 --> 00:15:11,000
Well

283
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:13,760
Don't misunderstand me

284
00:15:13,760 --> 00:15:17,060
You still have a ways to go before earning my approval

285
00:15:17,060 --> 00:15:19,420
Right

286
00:15:19,420 --> 00:15:20,840
Now then

287
00:15:20,840 --> 00:15:23,760
I'll overlook your insubordination this time

288
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:26,900
It was all this cowardly little idiot's doing in the first place

289
00:15:26,900 --> 00:15:28,680
What next?

290
00:15:28,940 --> 00:15:29,620
Your choice

291
00:15:29,620 --> 00:15:31,680
Shall we bring them to the capital?

292
00:15:32,440 --> 00:15:32,640
Hmm

293
00:15:32,640 --> 00:15:34,140
No

294
00:15:34,140 --> 00:15:36,940
I don't think that will be necessary

295
00:15:36,940 --> 00:15:38,940
Are you certain?

296
00:15:38,940 --> 00:15:43,060
As long as they never come near Hodge village again

297
00:15:43,060 --> 00:15:52,020
Those are our terms

298
00:15:52,020 --> 00:15:54,340
Now make yourselves scarce

299
00:15:54,340 --> 00:15:56,780
And never repeat this folly

300
00:15:56,780 --> 00:15:59,080
Do you understand?

301
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:00,080
Do you understand?

302
00:16:00,080 --> 00:16:02,080
You stupid commoner

303
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:06,480
Making you lose your guard like this was all part of the plan

304
00:16:06,480 --> 00:16:07,080
Huh?

305
00:16:07,080 --> 00:16:09,080
Holy lightning rising Zalim

306
00:16:09,080 --> 00:16:09,820
Water creation magic

307
00:16:09,820 --> 00:16:11,360
Holy fist of love

308
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:16,060
Behave yourself

309
00:16:16,060 --> 00:16:18,120
And try showing some remorse

310
00:16:18,120 --> 00:16:20,060
That goes for you too

311
00:16:20,060 --> 00:16:20,860
Yes, ma'am

312
00:16:20,860 --> 00:16:25,700
I think perhaps we should consider recruiting her into the magic nights

313
00:16:25,700 --> 00:16:27,940
Now

314
00:16:27,940 --> 00:16:30,860
There's been a change of plans

315
00:16:30,860 --> 00:16:32,280
We will be taking them in

316
00:16:32,280 --> 00:16:34,780
But first

317
00:16:34,780 --> 00:16:36,980
Tell me where the other one went

318
00:16:36,980 --> 00:16:49,160
Now that's my idea of a good time

319
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:53,460
I was ready to step in if it looked like things were getting dicey

320
00:16:53,460 --> 00:16:55,460
But they handled it just fine without me

321
00:16:55,460 --> 00:16:59,460
William's new recruits are certainly nothing to be ashamed of

322
00:16:59,460 --> 00:17:01,460
Not at all

323
00:17:01,460 --> 00:17:03,460
How long were you planning to lay the belt?

324
00:17:03,460 --> 00:17:05,460
Do you know how loud you are?

325
00:17:05,460 --> 00:17:07,460
You need to return immediately

326
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:09,460
There is a mountain of work to be done

327
00:17:09,460 --> 00:17:11,460
All right, all right

328
00:17:11,460 --> 00:17:13,460
At this rate you're gonna give yourself an ulcer

329
00:17:13,460 --> 00:17:15,460
And whose fault do you think that is?

330
00:17:17,460 --> 00:17:19,460
You're really back

331
00:17:19,460 --> 00:17:21,460
I'm so glad that you're okay

332
00:17:21,460 --> 00:17:23,460
So glad, so glad

333
00:17:23,460 --> 00:17:25,460
I guess we shouldn't be surprised

334
00:17:25,460 --> 00:17:27,460
Not with magic nights on the case

335
00:17:27,460 --> 00:17:28,460
Thank you all

336
00:17:28,460 --> 00:17:30,460
Mimosa, Klaus

337
00:17:30,460 --> 00:17:32,460
And lucky you two were there as well

338
00:17:32,460 --> 00:17:34,460
Think nothing of it

339
00:17:34,460 --> 00:17:37,460
We have the culprit, that cowardly fool

340
00:17:37,460 --> 00:17:39,460
Honestly, what was he thinking?

341
00:17:39,460 --> 00:17:40,460
Oh, right

342
00:17:40,460 --> 00:17:41,460
Please help yourselves

343
00:17:41,460 --> 00:17:44,460
The least that we can do is feed you before you go

344
00:17:44,460 --> 00:17:47,460
They may be a bit cold, but you can have as much as you'd like

345
00:18:04,460 --> 00:18:07,460
The flavor's not so bad, really

346
00:18:07,460 --> 00:18:10,460
I thought magic nights weren't supposed to lie, sir

347
00:18:10,460 --> 00:18:11,460
Hm

348
00:18:11,460 --> 00:18:15,460
Perfect

349
00:18:15,460 --> 00:18:18,460
Perfect

350
00:18:18,460 --> 00:18:28,460
A star?

351
00:18:28,460 --> 00:18:29,420
A star?

352
00:18:30,140 --> 00:18:34,940
The Wizard King has evaluated your deeds, and he has seen fit to grant you a star.

353
00:18:35,480 --> 00:18:38,500
Thank you, Captain. We're honored to receive it.

354
00:18:39,020 --> 00:18:43,040
Oh, wow. How many people can say they got a star on their very first mission?

355
00:18:43,560 --> 00:18:47,640
Although, I don't recall doing anything that extraordinary.

356
00:18:48,240 --> 00:18:52,120
On the contrary, Selim's testimony was quite valuable.

357
00:18:52,900 --> 00:18:56,340
Thanks to that, Congressman Hapshats' wrongdoings have all come to light.

358
00:18:57,060 --> 00:18:59,700
Bribery, fraudulent accounting, shadowy deals.

359
00:19:00,240 --> 00:19:04,280
Everyone involved has been rounded up, and you get all the credit.

360
00:19:05,400 --> 00:19:09,380
I wonder, sir, did you accept this mission, having anticipated such an outcome?

361
00:19:10,980 --> 00:19:16,200
Evil deeds must not go unpunished in the Clover Kingdom. It is our duty to see to that.

362
00:19:16,580 --> 00:19:17,040
Yes, sir.

363
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:24,360
Klaus, you know, Mimosa. I look forward to seeing what you will accomplish in the future.

364
00:19:24,360 --> 00:19:26,220
Sir.

365
00:19:26,340 --> 00:19:26,640
Sir.

366
00:19:28,080 --> 00:19:34,900
You know Mimosa. As far as new recruits go, well, they seem capable, I suppose.

367
00:19:40,420 --> 00:19:46,800
I expect a great deal. Oh, yes. Especially from you, you know.

368
00:19:46,800 --> 00:19:53,320
A star. Things turned out quite well in the end.

369
00:19:54,700 --> 00:19:58,300
But, you know, don't ever go off on your own again.

370
00:19:59,820 --> 00:20:00,260
Right.

371
00:20:01,060 --> 00:20:04,080
Why did you pause? Come on, you know, look at me.

372
00:20:04,320 --> 00:20:08,020
I want you to look me in the eye now and promise me that you won't do it again.

373
00:20:08,260 --> 00:20:08,700
Sure.

374
00:20:09,120 --> 00:20:12,220
You know? Hey, wait! You know!

375
00:20:12,220 --> 00:20:19,320
What? The Golden Dawn got a star? I can't believe it!

376
00:20:19,820 --> 00:20:21,660
Take us to your leader, Jubins.

377
00:20:21,860 --> 00:20:24,940
Justin, we finally got down to a hundred star difference, too.

378
00:20:25,240 --> 00:20:27,860
Well, it looks like we're back up to 101 now.

379
00:20:27,860 --> 00:20:33,340
No way! We were totally catching up to them, too!

380
00:20:33,580 --> 00:20:34,760
Yeah, we were close.

381
00:20:35,320 --> 00:20:37,680
No, sir. Not even slightly close.

382
00:20:38,360 --> 00:20:40,280
Really, our total's at negative 30.

383
00:20:40,520 --> 00:20:42,240
Take us to your leader, Jubins.

384
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:43,180
Shut that thing up!

385
00:20:43,620 --> 00:20:45,400
They won't be in the lead for long.

386
00:20:45,800 --> 00:20:48,740
It's just 101 stars. We'll catch up soon!

387
00:20:48,740 --> 00:20:51,200
I'm coming for you, Golden Dawn!

388
00:20:51,960 --> 00:20:52,960
You know!

389
00:21:07,040 --> 00:21:09,360
Sorry to interrupt, but there's urgent news, sir.

390
00:21:09,380 --> 00:21:11,620
We have a situation on our hands, yes?

391
00:21:13,120 --> 00:21:14,680
Calm down, Marks.

392
00:21:14,980 --> 00:21:16,840
The timing couldn't be more perfect.

393
00:21:16,840 --> 00:21:19,400
I know just who to give this mission to.

394
00:21:19,700 --> 00:21:20,480
Who, sir?

395
00:21:20,480 --> 00:21:21,480
Haha.

396
00:21:21,480 --> 00:21:21,980
Haha.

397
00:21:32,980 --> 00:21:37,180
誰もここから出られない

398
00:21:37,180 --> 00:21:45,160
閉じた狭い教室で

399
00:21:45,160 --> 00:21:51,340
今日も主役が輝いた

400
00:21:51,340 --> 00:21:59,960
僕は眩しくて目を閉じる

401
00:21:59,960 --> 00:22:06,800
散々考えた革命は手の中に

402
00:22:06,800 --> 00:22:08,880
おかしいだろう

403
00:22:08,880 --> 00:22:14,020
笑いたければ笑えばいいから

404
00:22:14,020 --> 00:22:18,360
残された僕らは

405
00:22:18,360 --> 00:22:21,880
何かになりたくて

406
00:22:21,880 --> 00:22:23,220
いつまでも

407
00:22:23,220 --> 00:22:24,960
いつまでも

408
00:22:24,960 --> 00:22:28,740
同じ朝を迎えてる

409
00:22:28,740 --> 00:22:32,380
明日を選ぶのは

410
00:22:32,380 --> 00:22:36,020
君自身しかいないよ

411
00:22:36,020 --> 00:22:37,400
超えていこう

412
00:22:37,400 --> 00:22:40,020
今日までの僕らを

413
00:22:40,020 --> 00:22:55,940
ご視聴ありがとうございました

414
00:22:55,940 --> 00:22:57,940
Clover Clips!

415
00:22:59,940 --> 00:23:00,940
My Chariot.

416
00:23:03,940 --> 00:23:05,940
Well, pretty impressive, is it not?

417
00:23:05,940 --> 00:23:08,940
The whole thing is nothing less than a marvel of craftsmanship.

418
00:23:08,940 --> 00:23:09,940
Pure perfection.

419
00:23:09,940 --> 00:23:10,940
Yeah, sure.

420
00:23:10,940 --> 00:23:14,940
I mean, its majesty practically screams Golden Dawn, don't you think?

421
00:23:14,940 --> 00:23:15,940
Yeah.

422
00:23:16,940 --> 00:23:17,940
Amazing!

423
00:23:17,940 --> 00:23:18,940
What is this thing?

424
00:23:18,940 --> 00:23:21,940
It's almost as awesome as the crazy cyclone!

425
00:23:21,940 --> 00:23:25,940
I think it could even give HaHa's wicked shooting star a run for its money!

426
00:23:25,940 --> 00:23:26,940
You'd better believe it.

427
00:23:26,940 --> 00:23:29,940
I don't know who you are, strange boy, but thank you.

428
00:23:30,940 --> 00:23:31,940
Are you leaving yet?

429
00:23:35,940 --> 00:23:37,940
What? Clear out a dungeon?

430
00:23:37,940 --> 00:23:39,940
Me, Asta, and Luck? It'll be fine.

431
00:23:39,940 --> 00:23:42,940
I can handle one measly dungeon no problem.

432
00:23:43,940 --> 00:23:46,940
Black Clover. Page 14. Dungeon.

433
00:23:46,940 --> 00:23:48,940
My magic is never giving up.

